00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.120
Here's your Tesla news rundown.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.040
Tesla's new patent lets GPUs pull only the exact frames needed for training,

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.420
cutting wasted decode time at petabyte scale.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:24.980
Tesla added a dedicated cleaning robot to the official scope of work

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.380
for its RoboTaxi hub in Austin.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.240
The inclusion signals that interior and exterior maintenance will be handled on-site

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.440
rather than through external services.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.360
This step fits into the broader preparation for unsupervised operations

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.560
by keeping the vehicle fleet in continuous rotation.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.820
Listeners tracking the RoboTaxi program will want to watch how the cleaning system

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.360
integrates with the hub's layout and daily throughput targets.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.420
The move keeps maintenance inside the operation so vehicles spend less time out of service.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.060
That operational choice connects directly to the data efficiency work that will power those

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:10.020
same vehicles. The filing describes a method that reads frame headers and timestamps without

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.300
full decoding, then isolates only the reference chain needed for requested moments.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.400
Multiple hardware decoders on the GPU can handle separate camera streams or training

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:27.040
batches in parallel. Intermediate frames are discarded once their features are extracted,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.460
leaving only the target images in local memory.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:37.140
The approach directly targets the data efficiency bottleneck in scaling both FSD and

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.560
Optimus training. Training data for vision models has long been treated as a continuous

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.180
stream that must be fully unpacked before any learning occurs.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:52.180
Tesla's recent patent instead treats the compressed bit stream as an indexed map,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:58.400
letting the GPU locate and decode only the frames a given training step actually requests.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:05.740
The result is a measurable drop in decode cycles per useful image, which matters once fleet video

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:12.560
reaches petabyte volumes. Lower per step cost directly improves the economics of running larger models

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.560
or more frequent updates without proportional increases in silicon or power.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.580
The same logic applies to Optimus training, where multiple camera angles and repeated task

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:29.920
demonstrations generate similar volumes of redundant footage. By discarding intermediate reference

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:35.460
frames once their features are extracted, the system keeps only the target images resident

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:41.140
in GPU memory. That discipline compounds across thousands of parallel sessions.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:47.380
Over time, the efficiency gains shifts the constraint from how much video can we afford to decode,

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.980
to how quickly can we label and curate the frames that matter.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:56.940
The next generation inference silicon reached tape out at Samsung's Taylor facility.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:04.160
The two nanometers node is intended to deliver higher performance per watt than the current HW4 package.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.840
Vehicle integration and dojo cluster compatibility remain the next milestones.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.440
Production volumes will determine how quickly the new silicon reaches customer fleets.

